Date: Sat, 25 Jul 2026 03:48:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] S3 completeness: all fourteen families on one command.
 14-entry ALL_FAMILIES registry with a coverage guard that ABORTS naming any
 family neither queued nor satisfied by a CSV stamped for the current
 input_sha (transitive F10 detection; stale legacy CSVs rejected). F0 added to
 the chunk queue on the combo axis via module-global combinations override
 (slicing all_features would have scanned 0.56%); MIN_TRADES overridden 10->30
 and MIN_PF kept at the loosened 2.0, both as module-globals so the ratified
 scanner stays byte-identical. F0's global 80% overlap dedup moved to
 collation over the assembled raw survivor set in ascending chunk order,
 reproducing single-pass semantics. F12 and F13 run as their own diagnostic
 stages honouring --workers, with F13's native shard checkpointing preserved.
 F0 pool asymmetry recorded in a sidecar note. QUICK_START: fourteen families,
 withdrawn ETA.

